This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

Two of the rule's three shapes apply, either alone being sufficient.

Its SUBJECT is scripts/validate-backlog-size.sh, which is not installed: install.sh's copy
loop derives from core/scripts/ and never touches the repo-root scripts/. Its CORPUS is
docs/backlog.md, this repository's own carry-over backlog, and a consumer tree gets no
docs/backlog.md at all. On a consumer this fixture would resolve no validator and no ledger,
and could only pass -- a unit that cannot fail scores as a pass in the consumer's own suite
verdict.

It also reads scripts/backlog-reverify.sh, scripts/backlog-rotate.sh and docs/backlog.md
directly for its three join probes (b15, b16, b17), which bind the ceiling's entry predicate to
the shipping classifier's population and to the rotator's own backlog_entry_label(). None of
those three exists on a consumer either.

The consumer's equivalent ledger is the push-candidate ledger under
_bmad-output/ai-dlc-update/, whose own fixtures (ledger-reverify, ledger-rotate,
ledger-status-vocabulary, ledger-reverify-unfalsifiable) ship and cover it. This one must not
be confused for those, and its siblings core/fixtures/backlog-ledger/ and
core/fixtures/backlog-rotate-fence-guard/ carry the same declaration for the same reason.
